Code motion (loop-invariant computation) 6.3 Loops




 DEFINITION

 Code motion (loop-invariant code motion / frequency reduction): move a computation whose value does not change in the loop to before the loop, so it is
 executed once instead of every iteration. Conditions: operands not modified in the loop; no side effects.



BEFORE AFTER

 while (a > 0) { x = y + z;
 x = y + z; while (a > 0) {
 if (a % x == 0) if (a % x == 0)
 printf(a); printf(a);
 a--; a--;
 } }


BEFORE AFTER

 for (j = 0; j < n; j++) { x = y + z;
 x = y + z; for (j = 0; j < n; j++)
 a[j] = 6 * j; a[j] = 6 * j;
 }


