Strength reduction 6.3 Loops




 DEFINITION

 Strength reduction: replace an expensive operation by a cheaper one (multiplication → addition / shift). Inside loops it
 is applied to induction variables.

BEFORE AFTER

 b = a * 2 b = a + a (or a << 1)
 b = a / 2 b = a >> 1
 x = y ^ 2 x = y * y

BEFORE AFTER

 for (i = 0; i < n; i++) { t = 0;
 t = 4 * i; for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
 A[t] = 0; A[t] = 0;
 } t = t + 4;
 }

