Loop unrolling 6.3 Loops




 DEFINITION

 Loop unrolling: replicate the loop body several times so the loop test and branch run fewer times. Best when
 the iteration count is known. Cost: larger code.

BEFORE AFTER

 i = 1; i = 1;
 while (i <= 100) { while (i <= 100) {
 X[i] = 0; X[i] = 0; i++;
 i++; X[i] = 0; i++;
 } }


 NOTE

 Unrolled by 2 ⇒ the test i <= 100 and the branch execute 50 times instead of 100.



