Loop jamming (fusion) 6.3 Loops




 DEFINITION

 Loop jamming / fusion: combine two loops that run the same number of times (and are independent) into
 one. Saves loop-control overhead and improves cache locality.

BEFORE AFTER

 for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
 a = a + i; a = a + i;
 for (j = 0; j < 10; j++) b = b + i;
 b = b + j; }




